---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const authorSituationResult = await authorSituation(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const interpretActionResult = await interpretAction(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, authorSituationResult.accepted);
const advanceWorldResult = await advanceWorld(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretActionResult.accepted);
const introduceChallengeResult = await introduceChallenge(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, advanceWorldResult.accepted);
const debriefPerformanceResult = await debriefPerformance(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, introduceChallengeResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { authorSituation: authorSituationResult, interpretAction: interpretActionResult, advanceWorld: advanceWorldResult, introduceChallenge: introduceChallengeResult, debriefPerformance: debriefPerformanceResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...authorSituationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...interpretActionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...advanceWorldResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...introduceChallengeResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...debriefPerformanceResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...authorSituationResult.checks, ...interpretActionResult.checks, ...advanceWorldResult.checks, ...introduceChallengeResult.checks, ...debriefPerformanceResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A learner asks an unexpected useful question: answer from world facts rather than rejecting it for not matching a script. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (answer from world facts rather than rejecting it for not matching a script.) through the existing stage result for PracticeScenario; preserve exact source/version and the prior PracticeScenario, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A network interruption occurs mid-turn: resume without duplicating the action. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (resume without duplicating the action.) through the existing stage result for PracticeScenario; preserve exact source/version and the prior PracticeScenario, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — An unsafe action is proposed: simulate refusal or consequences within the approved training policy, not real execution. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (simulate refusal or consequences within the approved training policy, not real execution.) through the existing stage result for PracticeScenario; preserve exact source/version and the prior PracticeScenario, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A scenario is reused: vary surface details while preserving its learning objective. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (vary surface details while preserving its learning objective.) through the existing stage result for PracticeScenario; preserve exact source/version and the prior PracticeScenario, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A learner succeeds by chance: distinguish final outcome from procedural competence. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (distinguish final outcome from procedural competence.) through the existing stage result for PracticeScenario; preserve exact source/version and the prior PracticeScenario, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, authorSituation: authorSituationResult, interpretAction: interpretActionResult, advanceWorld: advanceWorldResult, introduceChallenge: introduceChallengeResult, debriefPerformance: debriefPerformanceResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
